  "title": "BCCWJ-MEG",
  "description": "This dataset comprises magnetoencephalography (MEG) recordings from 35 Japanese native speakers reading newspaper articles presented word-by-word. Part of the BCCWJ-Brain collection, it enables cross-modality comparisons of language processing by providing high temporal resolution neural data acquired alongside fMRI and EEG from separate participant groups using identical stimuli. The dataset includes both raw and preprocessed MEG data, anatomical MRI, and detailed documentation of acquisition and analysis procedures.",
  "methods_description": "MEG data were acquired using a 200-channel whole-head MEG system with axial gradiometers at 1,000 Hz sampling rate with 200 Hz online low-pass filtering. Stimuli (20 Japanese newspaper articles) were presented word-by-word via rapid serial visual presentation (RSVP) at 500 ms per word with 500 ms inter-stimulus intervals. Preprocessing included CALM filtering, ICA-based artifact removal, 0.1–40 Hz bandpass filtering, epoching (−100 to 1,000 ms relative to word onset), downsampling to 200 Hz, and baseline correction. T1-weighted anatomical images were also acquired and defaced using PyDeface.",
